# payload-argv-lint-allow — exceptions to payload-argv-lint.sh, one extended regex per line,
# matched case-insensitively against "path/to/file.sh:LINE: <line text>".
#
# THIS FILE SHIPS EMPTY. Every JSON-named argv/env variable this fence has ever found in this
# tree was the real defect (law-payloads-go-on-stdin) — add a line here only for a variable
# the fence's heuristic cannot tell from one, never to silence a payload that is actually
# unbounded. Prefer fixing the call site (stdin, or a temp file's path) over adding a line.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# ADDED AT THE RUST CUTOVER (2026-09-29). spira-lint's payload-argv-lint parses commands
# rather than grepping one line, and found these the bash fence never saw. Each is bounded by
# something other than the bead store; each stays here only until its call site is fixed.
#
# Not payloads — the json-named variable holds a FILE PATH (the "filename-only" findings):
^spira/lib\.sh:[0-9]+: python3 .*bdsim\.py" "\$SPIRA_BDJSON_FIXTURE"
^spira/watchtower\.sh:[0-9]+: .*"\$_co_json_f" 2>/dev/null\)" \|\| _co_hits=""
# One bead's `bd show` JSON (lib.sh has_label-style check), bounded by one bead:
^spira/lib\.sh:[0-9]+: ' "\$label" "\$json" 2>/dev/null$
